  "distractor_rules": {
    "roots": [
      "The three bin labels stay fixed in this order: plural, singular possessive, plural possessive.",
      "Every stem is one clear noun form. A kid must not be able to read it two ways.",
      "Keep the filled pool near one third for each bin.",
      "Wrong-bin near misses use the same noun in another s form when you can: cats, cat's, cats'.",
      "Tier 1 uses short regular +s plurals and clear 's singular possessives.",
      "Tier 2 adds two-syllable nouns and regular plural possessives that end with s'.",
      "Tier 3 uses irregular plurals such as mice, children, men, geese, feet, or teeth, and their 's possessives.",
      "Stems use only the roots wordlist, allowed_extra_words, and <NAME>. No real names.",
      "Kid world only: school, home, food, pets, play, family, weather. No brands.",
      "Pictures are lemma_lookup notes only. Never invent audio files."
    ]
